params.body:
Performance pass on the showroom presentation (`showroom/{dealer_hash}`, the screen in the showroom that cycles through the vehicles; reloads every four hours and whenever the vehicle set changes). Analysed from the code; measurement snippet below to run before/after in the logged-in browser session.

**Causes found**
- `DealerController::showroom` (was line 297): without the Stocklist integration the vehicles were fetched with no eager load, while every slide reads `manufacturer`, `model`, `primary_stocklist_photo`, `fuel_type` and, through `trade_price_excl_vat`, `dealer->country`: five queries per vehicle, sixty vehicles deep. Now one eager load (`SHOWROOM_RELATIONS`); the integration branch gets `dealer.country` too.
- Line 304: `RealGarantService::isConnected($dealer_id)` = a live login at RealGarant during the page render, on a page a screen reloads on its own. Replaced by `isConfigured()` (database only), same standard as the detail page and the lists.
- `checkCarSet` (the every-15-minutes "did the set change?" call from every screen) loaded five relations to compare ids; relations dropped.
- Slides already lazy-load their photo (only the active and the next) and use the 960px WebP from the bucket; unchanged.

Timing marks added: `showroom_boot`, `showroom_vehicles`, `showroom_dealer_and_warranty`, `showroom_slides_view` (visible in Server-Timing for an administrator).

Expected: from about 5 queries x N vehicles plus one external login to about 8 queries and no external call; render time bounded by the slide template.

**Business rules written down** (docs/bedrijfsregels/12-s2, S2-7): 7.3 reworded (configured, not connected), new 7.6 price on a slide, 7.7 lease banner always on, 7.8 what a slide shows and ordering, 7.9 the change check. Findings X-74 (double margin for a colleague's margin vehicle: `showroom_vehicle.blade.php` adds `$marge` twice in the non-VAT branch), X-75 (`|| 1 == 1` shows the lease banner on every slide), X-76 (`check_cars()` reschedules only after a change). Behaviour deliberately unchanged in this PR; those three are questions for Ilse.

**Measurement (run in the browser console of the logged-in staging session, administrator)**
```js
const url = '/showroom/' + '<dealer_hash from the showroom link in settings>';
const r = await fetch(url, {credentials:'include', headers:{'X-Timing-Detail':'groups'}}); await r.text();
const st = r.headers.get('server-timing')||'';
const segs = [...st.matchAll(/(\w+);dur=([\d.]+)/g)].map(m=>m[1]+'='+Math.round(+m[2])).join(' ');
const groups = []; for (let k=1;k<=8;k++){ const h=r.headers.get('x-query-group-'+k); if(!h) continue; const m=h.match(/^(\d+)x (\d+)ms/); const t=(h.match(/from\s+`?(\w+)`?/i)||[])[1]||''; groups.push(m?m[1]+'x'+m[2]+'ms '+t.replace(/[aeiou]/g,'*'):'?'); }
console.log(segs, '|', groups.join(' ; '));
```
